openai-proof-research/frontier/campaigns/2026-10-27/new-discoveries-batch2/lanes/sol-fresh-source-discovery-r94/discovery.md:12:2. Same paper, Conjecture 2, PDF p6: for every iid log-concave real pair, h(sqrt(t)X+sqrt(1-t)Y) is concave on [0,1]. EXCLUDE PUBLIC REFUTATION. Luo arXiv:2609.11418v2 (14 September 2026), Theorems 1.1 and 1.2, supplies asymmetric and symmetric counterexamples respectively. The actual latest PDF is v2, despite search snippets describing only v1's asymmetric result. Its symmetric theorem already covers every signal fraction q>4/7. No rediscovery of that interval.
openai-proof-research/frontier/campaigns/2026-10-27/new-discoveries-batch2/lanes/sol-fresh-source-discovery-r94/discovery.md:20:Eskenazis–Gavalakis, actual author PDF of *On the entropy and information of Gaussian mixtures*, Section 2, Theorem 2 proof, formulas (20)–(24), establishes concavity using the entropy variational principle, Gaussian variance mixing, and concavity of -log g(sqrt(x)). That mechanism applies to variance mixtures and does not cover all symmetric log-concave densities. The nonlinear Gaussian-mixture representation is indispensable to its Jensen step.
